WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.850
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:15.120 --> 00:17.280
Our company just landed a major project

3
00:17.280 --> 00:18.560
worth tens of millions.

4
00:18.560 --> 00:21.640
So I’ll let Dan and Saint handle the project.

5
00:21.640 --> 00:23.160
Uh, Dan. Could you—

6
00:23.160 --> 00:24.040
Sorry.

7
00:24.040 --> 00:25.720
I don’t work outside office hours.

8
00:25.720 --> 00:26.720
Six o’clock sharp.

9
00:26.720 --> 00:27.920
Leave on time.

10
00:27.920 --> 00:28.720
Just you wait.

11
00:28.720 --> 00:30.720
I’m taking him down.

12
00:30.720 --> 00:32.360
SaintDan! SaintDan! SaintDan!

13
00:32.360 --> 00:33.520
Stop!

14
00:35.880 --> 00:36.960
I like…

15
00:36.960 --> 00:38.280
Don’t be afraid, Dan.

16
00:38.640 --> 00:41.280
I won’t let Kimhan do anything to my little brother.

17
00:51.240 --> 00:53.000
What I fear most in life…

18
00:53.440 --> 00:54.680
isn’t failure.

19
00:55.240 --> 00:56.920
It’s having the secret

20
00:56.920 --> 00:59.720
I’ve spent my whole life hiding

21
01:00.200 --> 01:01.600
getting exposed.

22
01:48.320 --> 01:51.160
And the person who holds most of my secret

23
01:51.440 --> 01:52.600
is…

24
01:52.840 --> 01:54.479
Good morning, Mr. Kimhan.

25
01:55.600 --> 01:56.880
Today you have a meeting

26
01:56.880 --> 01:59.160
about Siam Central Luxury Mall.

27
02:22.320 --> 02:23.640
Let’s get started.

28
03:46.240 --> 03:48.320
Uncle Kim!

29
03:49.240 --> 03:50.240
Yes?

30
03:50.680 --> 03:51.640
Hm?

31
03:52.680 --> 03:55.400
Why didn’t you tell me you were back?

32
03:55.400 --> 03:57.920
How long are you staying in Bangkok?

33
03:57.920 --> 03:59.640
Don’t go back to America, okay?.

34
03:59.640 --> 04:02.480
I want to play with you every day.

35
04:02.600 --> 04:04.040
Of course.

36
04:04.280 --> 04:06.920
Uncle will play with Gina every day.

37
04:07.080 --> 04:10.720
Can we get ice cream at our usual place?

38
04:11.800 --> 04:13.040
Okay.

39
04:13.560 --> 04:15.760
Pinky promise?

40
04:22.680 --> 04:23.440
Yay!

41
04:23.440 --> 04:25.440
You promised!

42
04:25.440 --> 04:30.680
I’ll dress up pretty and see you every day.

43
04:30.680 --> 04:31.960
Okay.

44
04:31.960 --> 04:33.200
See you.

45
04:45.800 --> 04:47.840
This time, I’m not going anywhere.

46
04:52.520 --> 04:53.600
So…

47
04:53.600 --> 04:55.080
About yesterday…

48
04:55.080 --> 04:56.840
I’m really sorry, Dan.

49
04:58.040 --> 04:59.080
Is it too lame?

50
04:59.080 --> 05:00.880
Dan, I’m sorry.

51
05:00.880 --> 05:02.880
Too casual?

52
05:02.880 --> 05:05.560
Dan, I really feel bad.

53
05:05.840 --> 05:09.040
I was too harsh.

54
05:09.320 --> 05:10.360
That won’t work.

55
05:11.360 --> 05:15.360
I’m sorry about what I said yesterday.

56
05:16.040 --> 05:17.800
I was too harsh.

57
05:17.800 --> 05:19.040
Will it take much longer?

58
05:20.280 --> 05:21.760
If it’ll take a while,

59
05:22.360 --> 05:23.600
let me put my bag down first.

60
05:27.680 --> 05:29.000
About yesterday,

61
05:30.280 --> 05:31.520
I’m sorry.

62
05:31.880 --> 05:33.280
I was too harsh.

63
05:33.760 --> 05:36.280
And I judged you without knowing you,

64
05:38.040 --> 05:42.240
or trying to talk thing through with you.

65
05:42.480 --> 05:43.640
I’m used to it.

66
05:45.000 --> 05:47.240
Everyone judges me by how I look.

67
05:51.720 --> 05:52.920
My bag.

68
05:52.920 --> 05:54.040
My clothes.

69
05:55.120 --> 05:56.280
My looks.

70
05:57.400 --> 05:58.400
And my car.

71
06:00.240 --> 06:01.400
Those things

72
06:01.920 --> 06:03.880
are easier to judge someone by

73
06:04.600 --> 06:06.920
than asking what they do,

74
06:08.200 --> 06:09.520
how they work,

75
06:10.440 --> 06:11.480
or what’s on their mind.

76
06:12.920 --> 06:14.880
Then can I ask you now?

77
06:16.400 --> 06:17.280
About what?

78
06:17.440 --> 06:19.040
How you work,

79
06:19.760 --> 06:22.040
and how you think.

80
06:22.320 --> 06:22.960
Oh.

81
06:23.160 --> 06:26.320
Let me buy you a coffee to make up for it.

82
06:36.040 --> 06:38.840
I’ve wanted to apologize since last night.

83
06:40.800 --> 06:42.040
I know.

84
06:44.600 --> 06:45.840
But just so you know,

85
06:46.520 --> 06:48.560
I’m pretty picky about coffee.

86
06:51.120 --> 06:53.000
That figures.

87
06:53.920 --> 06:54.720
Hey!

88
06:55.480 --> 06:57.280
You just apologized to me, remember?

89
07:01.040 --> 07:01.880
Yes.

90
07:02.600 --> 07:06.600
I’m trying to fix my bad habits.

91
07:10.600 --> 07:11.920
I’d like to order, please.

92
07:11.920 --> 07:14.640
A double-shot frappe latte

93
07:14.640 --> 07:17.160
with oat milk and whipped cream,

94
07:17.160 --> 07:19.520
drizzled with caramel and chocolate sauce,

95
07:19.520 --> 07:22.040
and extra almonds, please.

96
07:22.440 --> 07:24.280
-Sure. -Thank you.

97
07:26.400 --> 07:27.480
And I'll have...

98
07:27.880 --> 07:29.320
an iced Americano.

99
07:29.720 --> 07:32.360
Sure, that’ll be 375 baht.

100
07:37.640 --> 07:39.400
-Just a moment, please. -Thank you.

101
07:43.480 --> 07:44.760
Thanks for the coffee.

102
07:45.720 --> 07:47.080
Then I guess...

103
07:47.720 --> 07:49.159
we’re even.

104
07:51.240 --> 07:52.760
I’ve been thinking about it.

105
07:53.600 --> 07:55.320
This project means a lot to me.

106
07:55.880 --> 07:57.080
It’s a big project,

107
07:58.040 --> 08:00.240
and my chance to prove myself.

108
08:02.720 --> 08:04.400
I really want to do well.

109
08:04.760 --> 08:06.840
It means a lot to me too.

110
08:08.200 --> 08:09.320
Actually, at first,

111
08:09.600 --> 08:12.240
I even asked P’Ta to take me off this project.

112
08:13.200 --> 08:14.680
But she said

113
08:15.160 --> 08:16.960
the client specifically requested

114
08:16.960 --> 08:19.400
a top-selling AE like me.

115
08:21.320 --> 08:22.600
At least

116
08:23.120 --> 08:24.440
I get an opportunity

117
08:24.880 --> 08:27.080
to work with someone as good as you.

118
08:28.840 --> 08:31.240
Well, we’re stuck with each other.

119
08:32.880 --> 08:34.360
How about this?

120
08:35.400 --> 08:37.480
Let’s try to be good teammates.

121
08:40.919 --> 08:41.720
Deal?

122
08:47.720 --> 08:48.600
Deal.

123
08:59.080 --> 09:00.200
What’s with that look?

124
09:01.800 --> 09:02.920
We agreed

125
09:03.120 --> 09:04.720
to be good teammates, remember?

126
09:06.360 --> 09:07.800
Would a good teammate...

127
09:07.800 --> 09:10.440
dump this mountain of files on me?

128
09:10.440 --> 09:12.040
A good teammate

129
09:12.720 --> 09:14.720
just wants you to be prepared

130
09:14.720 --> 09:15.920
before the actual meeting.

131
09:19.880 --> 09:20.920
Good luck.

132
09:20.920 --> 09:21.880
Bye.

133
09:27.280 --> 09:30.040
What’s with him?

134
09:36.400 --> 09:37.360
Tomorrow,

135
09:38.040 --> 09:40.240
I’m taking down the top-selling AE.

136
09:41.720 --> 09:42.880
Just you wait.

137
09:43.920 --> 09:44.720
Ugh!

138
10:05.760 --> 10:08.200
Am I working or taking the bar exam?

139
10:19.000 --> 10:19.920
Ah!

140
10:22.360 --> 10:23.520
I thought you were a ghost.

141
10:24.800 --> 10:25.680
Dan.

142
10:26.840 --> 10:27.560
Here.

143
10:28.200 --> 10:29.600
I brought you some food

144
10:30.040 --> 10:33.080
to help you fight that mountain of paperwork.

145
10:33.480 --> 10:34.920
Easy now.

146
10:36.840 --> 10:37.760
Thank you.

147
10:39.640 --> 10:41.160
I’m not being nice.

148
10:41.840 --> 10:44.040
I’m just worried you won’t survive long enough

149
10:44.040 --> 10:45.640
to submit the work tomorrow.

150
10:47.560 --> 10:50.200
I thought I’d have to go on a ghost-hunting show.

151
11:13.960 --> 11:15.400
Uh…

152
11:18.120 --> 11:19.000
Here.

153
11:19.960 --> 11:20.520
Right here.

154
11:25.880 --> 11:26.640
What is it?

155
11:52.960 --> 11:54.200
Cilantro.

156
11:55.160 --> 11:57.000
You’ve got cilantro there.

157
11:57.160 --> 11:58.240
Thank you.

158
11:59.200 --> 12:00.440
It was starting to annoy me.

159
12:09.320 --> 12:10.800
I wanna go home already!

160
12:14.120 --> 12:15.320
You can't.

161
12:15.840 --> 12:16.880
We’re not done yet.

162
12:22.640 --> 12:23.880
And it’s due tomorrow.

163
12:28.080 --> 12:29.400
Then…

164
12:31.320 --> 12:33.000
Would you like to come work at my condo?

165
12:40.800 --> 12:41.960
This way.

166
12:53.840 --> 12:54.800
So…

167
12:55.080 --> 12:56.400
Where are we working?

168
12:56.840 --> 12:57.640
Over there.

169
13:02.720 --> 13:03.360
Sorry.

170
13:03.880 --> 13:06.280
My place is a bit small.

171
13:07.120 --> 13:09.200
It’s fine. The lighting’s just right.

172
13:15.160 --> 13:16.680
Take your time.

173
13:16.680 --> 13:18.160
I don’t mind.

174
13:33.080 --> 13:34.080
Here’s some water.

175
13:34.280 --> 13:35.280
Thanks.

176
13:46.360 --> 13:47.000
So…

177
13:47.960 --> 13:49.400
Where do I start?

178
13:50.080 --> 13:51.280
How far have you gotten?

179
13:51.960 --> 13:52.920
Let me see.

180
14:02.960 --> 14:03.680
Here.

181
14:04.440 --> 14:08.920
These are the visitor traffic figures for Siam Central.

182
14:09.200 --> 14:10.160
Well…

183
14:10.600 --> 14:15.200
High foot traffic doesn’t necessarily mean high sales.

184
14:17.000 --> 14:19.880
You need to find more sales data.

185
14:22.440 --> 14:23.280
Oh.

186
14:23.520 --> 14:24.240
Right.

187
14:24.600 --> 14:25.800
More research.

188
14:27.920 --> 14:29.520
Where did this figure come from?

189
14:30.360 --> 14:31.440
This one?

190
14:31.440 --> 14:34.720
It’s an estimate of Central’s customers’

191
14:34.720 --> 14:36.280
purchasing power.

192
14:37.600 --> 14:40.600
I’ll send you the file.

193
14:40.840 --> 14:42.720
It’ll give you a better idea.

194
14:52.080 --> 14:53.440
You’re more hardworking than I expected.

195
14:56.160 --> 14:59.240
I don’t want to look unprofessional.

196
15:00.800 --> 15:02.120
Then take a break.

197
15:02.120 --> 15:03.400
We still have plenty of time.

198
15:05.160 --> 15:07.640
Then you’ll dump another pile of files on me tomorrow.

199
15:08.960 --> 15:12.560
That depends on how hard you work tonight.

200
15:22.520 --> 15:23.120
Water.

201
15:25.320 --> 15:26.520
Let me refill it for you.

202
15:28.320 --> 15:28.640
Sure.

203
15:45.520 --> 15:46.640
Here you go.

204
15:47.840 --> 15:49.240
-Thank you. -You’re welcome.

205
16:03.360 --> 16:04.040
Hey.

206
16:04.800 --> 16:06.120
Are you okay?

207
16:06.720 --> 16:07.960
I’m fine.

208
16:09.080 --> 16:10.520
Never better.

209
16:12.000 --> 16:13.320
Why don’t you turn down the AC?

210
16:13.640 --> 16:15.160
You’re sweating.

211
16:18.960 --> 16:20.680
I get hot easily.

212
16:21.120 --> 16:22.520
I can tell.

213
16:22.960 --> 16:24.400
You turned down the AC at the office,

214
16:24.400 --> 16:25.880
and I was freezing.

215
16:28.840 --> 16:29.600
I just…

216
16:30.040 --> 16:31.440
don’t like being hot.

217
16:40.520 --> 16:41.160
Huh?

218
16:41.720 --> 16:42.360
Yeah?

219
16:44.520 --> 16:46.360
I’m gonna take a shower.

220
16:47.280 --> 16:47.880
A shower…

221
16:48.880 --> 16:49.680
might help me

222
16:50.520 --> 16:52.000
cool off a bit.

223
16:58.880 --> 17:00.080
He really gets hot easily.

224
19:40.760 --> 19:41.320
Hey!

225
19:41.760 --> 19:42.520
How’s it going?

226
19:43.040 --> 19:46.120
Burning the midnight oil with Prince Dan?

227
19:50.040 --> 19:50.840
How was it?

228
19:51.320 --> 19:53.120
Heavenly, huh?

229
19:53.560 --> 19:54.680
As if.

230
19:55.640 --> 19:57.720
And we didn’t work all night.

231
19:58.040 --> 19:59.880
What the heck?

232
20:00.600 --> 20:03.440
I thought you’d be exploding by now.

233
20:04.520 --> 20:06.680
Come on, let me see your face.

234
20:07.360 --> 20:11.280
So you actually survived Dan’s standards?

235
20:14.800 --> 20:15.720
Great!

236
20:16.200 --> 20:18.200
You passed Prince Dan’s probation test.

237
20:20.880 --> 20:23.720
How’s it working with him?

238
20:25.280 --> 20:26.120
Pretty good.

239
20:27.160 --> 20:28.520
Dan’s really talented.

240
20:29.800 --> 20:30.960
I put in the numbers,

241
20:30.960 --> 20:32.200
and Dan finds the insights.

242
20:32.960 --> 20:34.400
He’s so detail-oriented.

243
20:35.040 --> 20:37.520
Honestly, he’s more precise than AI.

244
20:40.280 --> 20:41.520
He keeps praising him.

245
20:41.880 --> 20:43.960
He isn't falling, right?

246
20:45.440 --> 20:47.040
I’m just appreciating his work.

247
20:49.160 --> 20:50.280
Looking good.

248
20:52.520 --> 20:52.920
Hey.

249
20:53.680 --> 20:54.120
Hey.

250
21:04.520 --> 21:05.960
Why don’t you let your hair down?

251
21:07.760 --> 21:09.200
It might look good.

252
21:14.360 --> 21:15.320
Like this.

253
21:34.520 --> 21:35.640
Much more handsome.

254
21:38.680 --> 21:39.440
Thank you.

255
21:40.320 --> 21:41.080
No problem.

256
21:41.200 --> 21:45.120
Just a little help from your mentor.

257
21:54.280 --> 21:56.840
Hold on. Let me gossip first.

258
21:57.720 --> 22:00.040
What’s the rush? Come join us.

259
22:03.560 --> 22:03.960
So...

260
22:04.160 --> 22:06.640
Our analysis of the target audience shows that

261
22:07.160 --> 22:08.800
interest in luxury lifestyles

262
22:08.800 --> 22:11.240
rose by 18% in Q3.

263
22:11.240 --> 22:13.760
How confident are you that it’ll exceed 18%?

264
22:14.480 --> 22:15.480
Very confident.

265
22:15.480 --> 22:17.720
We reviewed the Q1 and Q2 figures,

266
22:18.000 --> 22:19.480
and it shows steady growth.

267
22:20.000 --> 22:21.440
Our key message is

268
22:21.440 --> 22:24.280
‘Living above the ordinary’,

269
22:24.440 --> 22:26.840
which will be conveyed through sophisticated visuals.

270
22:28.320 --> 22:28.880
Dan.

271
22:29.280 --> 22:31.680
Why lead the presentation with visuals?

272
22:31.680 --> 22:33.200
Kimhan is coming back to Thailand.

273
22:35.200 --> 22:36.120
Why?

274
22:36.520 --> 22:38.000
Why is he suddenly coming back?

275
22:39.120 --> 22:42.120
He probably got tired of traveling on his parents’ money.

276
22:42.720 --> 22:43.480
Dan.

277
22:43.720 --> 22:46.320
Why lead the presentation with visuals?

278
22:50.000 --> 22:50.960
Dan?

279
22:54.160 --> 22:55.040
Uh…

280
22:57.720 --> 22:58.440
And Saint.

281
22:58.840 --> 23:01.200
Why include so much numerical detail?

282
23:03.520 --> 23:04.560
Just a moment, please.

283
23:07.280 --> 23:08.560
Please look into it.

284
23:09.880 --> 23:12.120
Tomorrow, we’re meeting the client at HQ.

285
23:12.280 --> 23:15.160
Every team, have your final sales presentation ready.

286
23:15.680 --> 23:17.440
Understood.

287
23:22.480 --> 23:23.320
Ow!

288
23:24.000 --> 23:24.760
What’s wrong?

289
23:28.720 --> 23:29.680
I got a cramp.

290
23:30.560 --> 23:31.440
I’m sorry.

291
23:33.040 --> 23:35.000
Relax. Don’t tense up.

292
23:47.680 --> 23:48.320
P’Ta.

293
23:48.320 --> 23:51.320
We’ve gathered all the information from our meetings

294
23:51.440 --> 23:56.160
and analyzed the strengths and weaknesses.

295
24:07.800 --> 24:08.800
Don’t worry.

296
24:09.840 --> 24:11.080
You can do this.

297
24:12.800 --> 24:13.920
I believe in you.

298
24:17.600 --> 24:19.040
Just go in there

299
24:20.000 --> 24:21.680
and be yourself.

300
24:22.440 --> 24:23.400
That’s enough.

301
24:24.200 --> 24:27.000
I’m not afraid of the work,

302
24:27.000 --> 24:28.920
It’s my past I’m afraid of.

303
24:29.680 --> 24:30.160
Mm.

304
24:30.960 --> 24:31.680
Thank you.

305
24:32.040 --> 24:32.600
Let’s go.

306
24:45.360 --> 24:46.120
Please have a seat.

307
24:48.840 --> 24:50.320
Shall we get started?

308
24:50.520 --> 24:51.440
One moment, please.

309
24:51.800 --> 24:53.040
We have one more person.

310
25:07.400 --> 25:09.520
Please welcome our new CEO,

311
25:09.520 --> 25:10.520
Mr. Kimhan.

312
25:10.520 --> 25:13.160
He’ll be joining us today.

313
25:14.240 --> 25:15.000
Hello.

314
25:15.600 --> 25:16.960
I’ve been looking forward…

315
25:17.720 --> 25:19.280
to today’s presentation.

316
25:19.760 --> 25:20.960
I hope you’ll do your best.

317
25:21.200 --> 25:21.680
Of course.

318
26:52.280 --> 26:53.920
Let’s get started.

319
26:54.840 --> 26:57.360
Our analysis of the target audience

320
26:57.840 --> 26:59.200
shows that

321
26:59.200 --> 27:00.680
interest in luxury lifestyles

322
27:00.680 --> 27:03.080
rose by 18% in Q3.

323
27:03.480 --> 27:05.000
Our key message is

324
27:05.320 --> 27:06.680
‘Living above the ordinary’,

325
27:06.880 --> 27:09.000
which will be conveyed through sophisticated visuals.

326
27:09.200 --> 27:13.720
We’ll shoot at iconic locations in Bangkok,

327
27:13.720 --> 27:16.120
using fast-paced camera movements

328
27:16.160 --> 27:18.440
to capture the urban lifestyle.

329
27:18.720 --> 27:22.560
Our communication strategy will maximize impact

330
27:22.560 --> 27:26.520
in both brand image and sales.

331
27:35.440 --> 27:35.840
And...

332
27:36.720 --> 27:38.120
In Q3,

333
27:38.360 --> 27:42.120
Siam Central department store saw sales grow 12.7%,

334
27:42.160 --> 27:45.200
compared to the same period last year.

335
27:45.440 --> 27:48.320
That’s well above

336
27:48.320 --> 27:51.920
the retail market average of just 7–8%.

337
27:52.560 --> 27:56.040
These figures show that the Siam Central campaign

338
27:56.160 --> 27:58.640
won’t just build brand awareness.

339
27:58.800 --> 28:01.200
It’ll also drive actual sales.

340
28:01.360 --> 28:02.960
Because our existing customers

341
28:02.960 --> 28:06.520
will become early adopters for our brand.

342
28:07.680 --> 28:10.520
All of this reinforces the idea

343
28:10.800 --> 28:12.720
that our department store

344
28:12.720 --> 28:14.800
is a place to experience life.

345
28:15.200 --> 28:16.960
And that’s why we’re confident

346
28:16.960 --> 28:19.200
that this campaign

347
28:19.720 --> 28:22.160
won’t just boost sales.

348
28:22.360 --> 28:24.120
It’ll also elevate our brand image

349
28:24.120 --> 28:27.920
as the country’s new hub for luxury lifestyles.

350
28:37.280 --> 28:38.320
I have a question.

351
28:39.920 --> 28:41.800
Q3 sales did increase.

352
28:43.360 --> 28:45.800
But online channels are growing much faster,

353
28:46.040 --> 28:49.240
Why do you think a luxury mall campaign

354
28:49.240 --> 28:50.520
can make a bigger impact

355
28:50.520 --> 28:52.120
than online media buying?

356
28:56.320 --> 28:57.080
Well…

357
29:06.800 --> 29:07.680
That’s a fair point.

358
29:10.240 --> 29:12.080
Let me answer your question, Mr. Kimhan.

359
29:14.160 --> 29:15.600
Online channels are growing fast,

360
29:15.600 --> 29:17.160
but if we look deeper,

361
29:17.160 --> 29:18.920
Siam Central’s customers

362
29:18.920 --> 29:21.160
are willing to pay for premium experiences.

363
29:22.160 --> 29:24.160
They’re not just looking at online reviews.

364
29:24.160 --> 29:25.800
They want an experience.

365
29:26.360 --> 29:28.560
They want to immerse themselves in luxury

366
29:28.560 --> 29:30.640
that fits their lifestyle.

367
29:30.800 --> 29:33.040
That’s something online shopping can’t replicate.

368
29:33.400 --> 29:35.600
The Q3 traffic figures

369
29:35.600 --> 29:38.840
showing a 20% increase are interesting.

370
29:40.880 --> 29:42.680
But how can you be sure

371
29:42.680 --> 29:44.320
that this increase in foot traffic

372
29:44.720 --> 29:46.440
will translate into actual sales,

373
29:47.120 --> 29:49.240
rather than people just browsing and leaving?

374
29:49.400 --> 29:50.040
That’s right.

375
29:50.880 --> 29:53.560
Traffic doesn’t guarantee sales.

376
29:54.840 --> 29:56.280
Most of that 20% growth

377
29:56.280 --> 29:58.760
comes from the high-spending segment,

378
29:58.760 --> 30:01.080
who are ready to buy,

379
30:01.080 --> 30:02.200
not just to window-shop.

380
30:02.200 --> 30:05.280
The mall’s data also shows that spending per head

381
30:05.280 --> 30:07.800
is almost twice the market average.

382
30:08.160 --> 30:10.520
If we offer products worthy of that setting,

383
30:10.960 --> 30:12.720
we’re not just selling products,

384
30:12.720 --> 30:14.320
but we’re selling a feeling.

385
30:14.720 --> 30:17.960
The feeling of living above the ordinary.

386
30:17.960 --> 30:19.280
And that feeling

387
30:19.280 --> 30:21.560
will turn foot traffic into actual customers.

388
30:28.280 --> 30:29.320
Excellent.

389
30:30.160 --> 30:32.560
That’s what they want to hear.

390
30:33.160 --> 30:34.240
Thank you.

391
30:51.400 --> 30:53.280
Alright. That's all for today.

392
30:53.800 --> 30:56.000
If you have any questions, come see me next week.

393
30:56.000 --> 30:56.880
Class dismissed.

394
31:07.600 --> 31:09.000
Professor.

395
31:09.320 --> 31:11.560
Thank you so much for today’s class.

396
31:11.560 --> 31:12.560
I really enjoyed it.

397
31:13.320 --> 31:16.400
I’ll ask you more about the assignment next week.

398
31:16.840 --> 31:18.600
Of course. See you then.

399
31:18.800 --> 31:20.520
-Goodbye. -Goodbye.

400
31:30.320 --> 31:32.120
(What are you doing?)

401
31:37.000 --> 31:38.360
(What are you planning now?)

402
31:47.600 --> 31:48.840
(You’ll find out soon.)

403
32:09.840 --> 32:10.560
P’Ta.

404
32:10.880 --> 32:12.600
The new CEO is so intense.

405
32:12.960 --> 32:16.320
I thought we were all doomed!

406
32:16.600 --> 32:17.600
I was shrinking.

407
32:17.600 --> 32:19.080
So tense.

408
32:19.280 --> 32:20.920
Really tense.

409
32:23.400 --> 32:25.000
I thought I wouldn’t make it either.

410
32:26.680 --> 32:28.880
Everyone did a great job.

411
32:28.880 --> 32:29.800
Especially Saint.

412
32:30.600 --> 32:32.480
Your answers were spot-on.

413
32:32.480 --> 32:34.200
They were really impressed.

414
32:34.200 --> 32:35.800
-Thank you. -Our team’s amazing.

415
32:36.080 --> 32:38.320
-Fantastic. -Good job, everyone.

416
32:46.360 --> 32:46.880
Dan.

417
32:49.680 --> 32:50.800
You did really well.

418
32:53.120 --> 32:53.560
Mm.

419
32:54.680 --> 32:56.560
I guess I did.

420
33:03.400 --> 33:04.800
Is Mr. Kimhan…

421
33:07.520 --> 33:08.800
what’s bothering you?

422
33:10.320 --> 33:10.920
No.

423
33:11.600 --> 33:12.600
I’m just a little tired.

424
33:13.800 --> 33:14.920
I’m gonna take a break.

425
33:15.720 --> 33:16.840
Need a ride?

426
33:20.160 --> 33:21.640
I noticed you didn’t drive today.

427
33:21.880 --> 33:22.720
It’s okay.

428
33:23.520 --> 33:24.480
I can get home on my own.

429
33:42.160 --> 33:43.520
The rain falling

430
33:45.000 --> 33:47.960
is nothing compared to the weight on my heart.

431
34:26.760 --> 34:28.480
Let me walk you to the station.

432
34:30.600 --> 34:32.080
so you don’t get wet.

433
34:37.080 --> 34:37.800
It’s okay.

434
34:39.400 --> 34:40.639
I want to go alone.

435
35:26.240 --> 35:27.320
Why are you so soaked?

436
35:41.400 --> 35:42.200
P’James.

437
35:46.200 --> 35:47.760
Do you know?

438
35:50.160 --> 35:52.560
The client for the major project I’m working on

439
35:55.800 --> 35:56.680
is…

440
35:57.680 --> 35:58.800
P’Kimhan.

441
36:03.880 --> 36:05.360
I don’t want him to come back.

442
36:10.280 --> 36:11.000
P’James.

443
36:16.960 --> 36:18.280
I like you.

444
36:19.680 --> 36:21.960
I’ve liked you since we first met.

445
36:24.960 --> 36:25.640
Hey!

446
36:26.400 --> 36:27.840
Watch where you’re going!

447
36:28.000 --> 36:28.920
I’m sorry.

448
36:29.200 --> 36:30.120
I didn’t mean to.

449
36:30.800 --> 36:31.840
Looking for trouble?

450
36:41.840 --> 36:43.600
You bumped into him first.

451
36:58.480 --> 37:01.400
You may not even remember when we first met.

452
37:02.200 --> 37:04.400
But I’ve always remembered.

453
37:07.120 --> 37:09.040
I’ve held on to that feeling

454
37:09.320 --> 37:12.520
and kept it a secret for over ten years.

455
37:15.200 --> 37:16.040
Dan.

456
37:21.640 --> 37:23.200
Thank you so much

457
37:25.360 --> 37:27.600
for telling me how you feel.

458
37:32.320 --> 37:33.520
I’m really glad

459
37:35.960 --> 37:37.560
to have you in my life.

460
37:39.760 --> 37:41.720
You mean a lot to me.

461
37:43.800 --> 37:45.680
I trust you

462
37:48.800 --> 37:50.640
and feel comfortable with you.

463
37:54.480 --> 37:55.960
But don’t you think...

464
38:01.960 --> 38:03.280
we’re better off

465
38:04.280 --> 38:05.560
just the way we are?

466
38:15.440 --> 38:17.120
Better off like this?

467
38:22.560 --> 38:24.160
What’s so good about it?

468
38:25.800 --> 38:27.600
I have to keep these feelings to myself.

469
38:27.880 --> 38:28.960
Keep them a secret.

470
38:30.160 --> 38:31.520
I can’t tell anyone.

471
38:32.240 --> 38:34.280
I can’t even tell you.

472
38:35.760 --> 38:37.880
I have to keep smiling as if there’s nothing,

473
38:39.480 --> 38:41.160
even though deep down,

474
38:41.720 --> 38:43.800
all I want is to tell you I love you.

475
38:44.040 --> 38:46.320
Please don’t make this any harder, Dan.

476
38:51.440 --> 38:52.960
I don’t want to lose you.

477
38:56.560 --> 38:58.920
I think if we cross that line,

478
39:00.680 --> 39:02.000
everything will fall apart.

479
39:03.400 --> 39:06.680
I’m not afraid of things falling apart.

480
39:08.160 --> 39:09.360
What I’m afraid of

481
39:10.480 --> 39:12.520
is not being able to stay by your side.

482
39:15.920 --> 39:17.080
Do you know...

483
39:17.640 --> 39:20.920
I’ve kept these words for ten years?

484
39:23.920 --> 39:25.120
And now,

485
39:27.600 --> 39:30.760
you’re telling me there’s no chance for us?

486
39:42.440 --> 39:44.080
I want you to be happy, Dan.

487
39:48.320 --> 39:51.080
But I can’t be the reason for it.

488
41:00.920 --> 41:02.040
Why are you here?

489
41:03.520 --> 41:04.640
If it’s not about work,

490
41:05.400 --> 41:06.680
don’t come to see me again.

491
41:08.760 --> 41:10.200
Shut up.

492
41:13.680 --> 41:15.440
I’m not your plaything anymore.

493
41:16.040 --> 41:17.520
If you have nothing else to say,

494
41:17.520 --> 41:18.600
I’m leaving.

495
41:18.760 --> 41:20.400
James.

496
41:26.320 --> 41:27.240
How’s it going?

497
41:27.360 --> 41:28.520
I’m exhausted.

498
41:29.840 --> 41:30.760
Your shirt’s wrinkled.

499
41:30.760 --> 41:31.680
Did you sleep in it?

500
41:31.680 --> 41:32.640
No.

501
41:32.640 --> 41:35.160
I ironed it already.

502
41:35.160 --> 41:36.360
Really?

503
41:36.360 --> 41:37.000
Mm.

504
41:40.000 --> 41:40.920
Can you stop?

505
41:43.440 --> 41:44.080
Why?

506
41:44.880 --> 41:46.560
Why is it always like this?

507
41:47.400 --> 41:48.400
Because...

508
41:51.280 --> 41:53.240
you can’t say no to me, can you?

509
41:55.720 --> 41:57.120
Stay away from P’James.

510
41:59.120 --> 42:00.440
And what do I get in return...

511
42:01.480 --> 42:03.080
if i do that?

512
42:08.480 --> 42:09.400
Everything.

513
42:11.000 --> 42:12.400
Everything you want.

514
42:13.680 --> 42:14.560
Like today.

515
42:15.280 --> 42:16.680
You wanted me to come here,

516
42:17.680 --> 42:18.680
so I did.

517
42:21.600 --> 42:22.160
Good.

518
42:23.800 --> 42:24.880
At least,

519
42:26.560 --> 42:28.000
now you know

520
42:28.000 --> 42:29.520
you can’t escape me.

521
43:09.880 --> 43:11.360
Where’s Dan?

522
43:14.200 --> 43:15.400
No idea.

523
43:15.640 --> 43:17.120
I haven’t seen him all morning.

524
43:19.640 --> 43:22.400
Maybe he’s secretly gone on a date.

525
43:23.320 --> 43:24.360
I doubt it.

526
43:24.360 --> 43:25.120
Ellie.

527
43:25.840 --> 43:26.120
Yes.

528
43:26.720 --> 43:29.040
Everyone, Dan called in sick today.

529
43:31.120 --> 43:31.640
Okay.

530
43:32.760 --> 43:34.320
Oh.

531
43:34.720 --> 43:35.840
Sick leave.

532
43:36.000 --> 43:37.640
I thought he’d snuck off on a date.

533
43:39.120 --> 43:40.040
Kinda sus.

534
43:40.440 --> 43:40.920
Right?

535
44:13.600 --> 44:13.880
Oh.

536
44:17.280 --> 44:17.920
That was quick.

537
44:48.280 --> 44:50.680
What I feared most had come back.

538
44:51.560 --> 44:52.640
P’Kimhan,

539
44:53.320 --> 44:55.880
the man who holds all my secrets.

540
44:57.160 --> 44:58.680
I’m not your plaything anymore.

541
44:58.680 --> 45:00.320
James.

542
45:01.320 --> 45:02.440
Stop,

543
45:02.440 --> 45:03.880
or I’ll expose your secret.

544
45:04.680 --> 45:06.520
Then I’ll expose yours first.

545
45:09.400 --> 45:11.080
Can I be someone you trust?

546
45:11.080 --> 45:13.560
Maybe I’m not who you think I am.

547
45:13.840 --> 45:15.680
He can afford designer brands

548
45:15.880 --> 45:17.360
because he’s a sugar baby!

549
45:17.360 --> 45:18.120
Whoa.

550
45:19.560 --> 45:20.920
Saint!

551
45:20.920 --> 45:21.520
Please stop!

552
45:21.520 --> 45:23.440
Keep this asshole out of our business!
